      "retained_memory": "Folded weight copies total 11,171,008 float32 elements (~44.7 MB) plus 20 folded bias vectors (2,752 floats, ~11 KB), retained in closures for the candidate lifetime on the CUDA device alongside the untouched originals (~44.7 MB). framework.lifecycle_peak_allocated_bytes and lifecycle_peak_reserved_bytes therefore rise by roughly the folded-copy size (setup/installation allocation, reported here, not hidden); framework.peak_allocated_bytes is reset per run but still reflects these steady-state live allocations during the forward, so the offline row's peak_allocated_bytes memory goal may report a slightly higher peak (activation buffers dominate the run peak). This counter increase is the accounting cost of retaining a folded copy, not a physical-memory saving claim; the request's latency_ms objective carries no memory constraint (the 0.95 images_per_second ratio belongs to the offline row's memory goal, and throughput improves with latency)."
